{"title":"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> has a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82364c4133ac9d84246adeb9045ab0369c177c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FA=FB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9f4cb8cd01ce230066f3ce5412abf38dc79b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=DC$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1cf3a489a4a75ba57664d86aa9382ebdbe4959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAB}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdb8a9795ba0241dfd42592e0da6b3ca3dfa9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=ED$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f4151f8ac9f951f798810698ab708d02e12795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408b1b1ac63afdc7c57374eb64a96a01ba86f11a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMXE$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616d05a6cb10d1b2c940889b98aa13157bd40ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD,FX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016IMOQ1.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a5/2016IMOQ1.jpg/800px-2016IMOQ1.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"434\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a5/2016IMOQ1.jpg/1200px-2016IMOQ1.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a5/2016IMOQ1.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ed/2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg/600px-2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"355\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ed/2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg/900px-2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ed/2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg/1200px-2016IMOQ1Solution.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The Problem shows that \\(\\angle DAC = \\angle DCA = \\angle CAD\\), it follows that \\(AB \\parallel CD\\). Extend \\(DC\\) to intersect \\(AB\\) at \\(G\\), we get \\(\\angle GFA = \\angle GFB = \\angle CFD\\). Making triangles \\(\\triangle CDF\\) and \\(\\triangle AGF\\) similar. Also, \\(\\angle FDC = \\angle FGA = 90^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle FBC = 90^\\circ\\), which points \\(D\\), \\(C\\), \\(B\\), and \\(F\\) are concyclic.\n</p><p>And \\(\\angle BFC = \\angle FBA + \\angle FAB = \\angle FAE = \\angle AFE\\). Triangle \\(\\triangle AFE\\) is congruent to \\(\\triangle FBM\\), and \\(AE = EF = FM = MB\\). Let \\(MX = EA = MF\\), then points \\(B\\), \\(C\\), \\(D\\), \\(F\\), and \\(X\\) are concyclic.\n</p><p>Finally \\(AD = DB\\) and \\(\\angle DAF = \\angle DBF = \\angle FXD\\).  \\(\\angle MFX = \\angle FXD = \\angle FXM\\) and \\(FE \\parallel MD\\) with \\(EF = FM = MD = DE\\), making \\(EFMD\\) a rhombus. And \\(\\angle FBD = \\angle MBD = \\angle MXF = \\angle DXF\\) and triangle \\(\\triangle BEM\\) is congruent to \\(\\triangle XEM\\), while \\(\\triangle MFX\\) is congruent to \\(\\triangle MBD\\) which is congruent to \\(\\triangle FEM\\), so \\(EM = FX = BD\\).\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Athmyx\">Athmyx</a>\nnote: i believe the first paragraph is flawed\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f47c30d6217616fa450b56cd8a25384ae3524ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBA = \\angle FAB = \\angle FAD = \\angle FCD = \\angle DAE = \\angle ADE = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"496\" height=\"14\" />. And WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00ae454a821fab63e745f9146bae60a2d184ef72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a52878ef3ae00b841bcead1029e2440ccfe2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f7fc7b8ac643979ffd3c405b20d5869e85b6bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = CF.cos(2\\alpha) = 2.cos(2\\alpha) = FA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901e7098ecb23fbfc82fa23f335e63c835b17e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = \\frac{AC}{2cos(\\alpha)} = \\frac{CF+FA}{2cos(\\alpha)} = \\frac{2+2cos(2\\alpha)}{2cos(\\alpha)} = \\frac{1+cos(2\\alpha)}{cos(\\alpha)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"475\" height=\"45\" /> and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fadc159966ca951f4db4c69647ac9d59ac35d737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = AE = \\frac{DA}{2cos(\\alpha)} = \\frac{1+cos(2\\alpha)}{2.(cos(\\alpha))^2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"326\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c0b0f5678567ad5b5f3946093120dfeace261e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX = DE = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25c5de391dbdaeb4650ac4cb297a4a07a7be630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE  ||  MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c9045545108f9231b6bdfc85820083b3336f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 1 = MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />, so we conclude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8f611439ef86631ecd31b86f71d3e9033be827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is parallelogram. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afc277e80311b3c2d592dc8e14d90bf3f19445b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AME = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5ccc66838cb5ada0f3a06cdb2d469bf2472d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MDEA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> is isosceles trapezoid. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/4989ab93e13212a52760ace7978926c255c01a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD = EA = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />. By basic angle chasing, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48682502cc72876a58be948a38bec4dff9f3f162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MBF = \\angle MFB = 2\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21809463c718785ae0bd202dd4cc24819502184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MXD = \\angle MDX = 2\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"200\" height=\"14\" /> and we have seen that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0514bdaf047bf5d37e0d1cd9cc1aa608e96cfafe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB = MF = MD = MX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"214\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0e429456c3f45b3875e502bc444131e0b568a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFDX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is isosceles trapezoid. And we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd033186356cb53af65c6bfd667852eab9035358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FMD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the symmetrical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0e429456c3f45b3875e502bc444131e0b568a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFDX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetrical respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Hence, the symmetry of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875c1abb181a739a3ba2f3e74a6511b98ef39073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />. And we are done <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~EgeSaribas\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO\" title=\"2016 IMO\">2016 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222456\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 332/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10321/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.982      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.982      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17556:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017222456 and revision id 261413. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}